{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-006", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh's import bill rises 11.5% in Q1 FY27", "content": "Bangladesh’s import payments rose 11.50 per cent year-on-year to $18.91 billion in Q1 FY27, while new letters of credit climbed nearly 22 per cent to $22.46 billion.\nPetroleum imports increased nearly 28 per cent, but industrial raw material imports fell 1.80 per cent and capital machinery was almost unchanged.\nBangladesh Bank officials expect obligations to rise ahead of Ramadan.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-import-bill-rises-11-5-in-q1-fy27-314887-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-007", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Trade bodies of Bangladesh & Russia sign investment pact", "content": "Bangladesh's FBCCI and the Russia-Bangladesh Business Council have signed an MoU in Dhaka to remove barriers and expand investment and business cooperation.\nBilateral trade is nearly $2 billion, with Bangladesh exporting ready-made garments, jute and leather goods to Russia.\nOfficials cited regulatory, logistics and payment infrastructure gaps, while Russia also sees scope in oil and gas.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/trade-bodies-of-bangladesh-russia-sign-investment-pact-314886-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-008", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam’s T&A sector: Making business case for going green", "content": "Vietnam’s textile and apparel manufacturers are turning to cleaner production as energy costs hit $3 billion a year and buyers demand responsible sourcing.\nProjects include Spectre’s $30 million LEED Gold factory, Tan De’s 11 MWp rooftop solar and recycling at Thanh Cong Textile and Garment.\nGovernment programmes support the shift, but smaller firms face financing, technology and expertise gaps.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-t-a-sector-making-business-case-for-going-green-314872-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-009", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase", "expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Kontoor Brands posts 40% jump in Q3 adjusted EPS", "content": "Kontoor Brands raised its FY26 adjusted EPS outlook to $5.40 after Q3 revenue rose 3 per cent to $685 million and adjusted EPS increased 40 per cent to $1.50.\nAdjusted gross margin expanded 230 basis points to 48.1 per cent, supported by Project Jeanius, pricing and favourable business mix.\nFollowing the Lee divestiture, the US apparel group expects adjusted EPS of at least $6.60 in 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-kontoor-brands-posts-40-jump-in-q3-adjusted-eps-314888-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-09-010", "date": "2026-11-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["expand", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Norway's apparel imports rise 6%, signalling focus on affordability", "content": "Norway’s apparel imports rose 6.39 per cent year on year to $1.614 billion in January–August 2026, signalling recovery after a 2025 contraction.\nAverage import values declined as garment volumes expanded, pointing to more price-conscious sourcing and value-for-money buying.\nChina and Bangladesh supplied $824.164 million, or 51.05 per cent of imports; Turkiye, Vietnam and India followed.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/norway-s-apparel-imports-rise-6-signalling-focus-on-affordability-314837-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
